# added src/superclaude references in installed primitives and plugin mirrors since HEAD
+1. Reads the routing guide first (`~/.claude/HOW-WE-WORK.md`, else the skill's `refs/HOW-WE-WORK.md` in a plugin install, else `src/superclaude/core/HOW-WE-WORK.md`; inside an IronClaude checkout, where `src/superclaude/commands/` exists under `git rev-parse --show-toplevel`, the `src/` copy is read first). It matches the whole requested outcome (deliverable, explicitly named command or existing artifact, compatible mode/depth/output choices and how much it may change) to one routing row, not any single phrase. A matched row's applicable steps are returned in order, with exactly one selected alternative and their verified flags, and stop at the requested deliverable: a report-only or plan-only request gains no execution, commit or push step. If the objective stays ambiguous, it asks one question and stops. No hand-written keyword table.
+1. **Spawn the cold-path Haiku subagent.** Read `COLD_PATH_RUNBOOK` from `src/superclaude/cli/recommend/prompts.py` only inside the verified IronClaude checkout, then use that condensed text rather than the full skill body. Pass the verbatim current request, the classifier's existing key (or `unknown`), guide status/path and level/Other-command blocks, the guide's relevant lifecycle guidance, and resolved reference paths from the current skill directory. The worker performs live enumeration/ranking/verification and constructs a request-specific handoff. It may return `cache_update` with the existing fields (`key`, `candidate`, `flags`, `prompt_envelope_template`, `rationale`, `source_path`, `native_fallback`) only for an eligible target and an existing compatible classification key. Unknown/ambiguous objectives do not invent keys or force ordinary planning into task-file-generation; emit the verified result without insertion. If the runbook cannot be read, run Phase 0-2 inline and skip cache/eval helpers. Before any emission, the parent checks current objective, authority, verification evidence and parameter binding; the worker's text is not unconditionally surfaced verbatim.
+| In-checkout research fallback | `src/superclaude/commands/*.md`, `src/superclaude/skills/*/SKILL.md`, `src/superclaude/agents/*.md`, `src/superclaude/templates/**/*.md`, `src/superclaude/examples/*-template.md` | Only when these exist under the current IronClaude git root |
+5. The routing guide's canonical copy is `src/superclaude/core/HOW-WE-WORK.md`. When you change it, recopy its level-table block into `src/superclaude/core/CLAUDE.md` and copy the whole file byte-for-byte to `plugins/superclaude/skills/sc-recommend/refs/HOW-WE-WORK.md` (tests check both). The routing and recommendation tests are static text and cache checks: they pin the written contract, not which route a model actually picks. When routing behavior changes, check it with a separate recorded model-generation evaluation and report those results apart from the static tests.
+6. Inside a command, never point at another primitive with a `src/superclaude/...` path. The installed copy is what runs in other projects, so name `~/.claude/skills/<name>/SKILL.md`, `~/.claude/agents/<name>.md` or `~/.claude/commands/sc/<name>.md` (and accept the project `.claude/` copy where a lookup needs it). See the "Never Hardcode `src/superclaude/` Paths" rule in the repository `CLAUDE.md`.
